\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Comparison with published MemoryAgentBench, LoCoMo, and LongMemEval-S results. Each block lists its answerer, judge, subset, and test procedure; published rows are from Hu et al.~\citep  {hu2025memoryagentbench}, Chhikara et al.~\citep  {chhikara2025mem0}, and Rasmussen et al.~\citep  {rasmussen2025zep}. In (b), the weighted column is recomputed from published category means under the 841/282/96/321 counts; cross-block rows use different protocols and are background, not controlled comparisons. Our MAB rows use the Align+ extended sample ($n{=}1074$, 14 task groups; \cref  {app:sampling}); the same-model full-context row is a reference at 614/1{,}074 coverage, rather than a competing system, and its margin over the source-reading agent ($-7.9$ points, 95\% CI $[-11.9,-3.9]$) is analyzed in \cref  {sec:ladder}. LRU has only $n{=}14$ questions, including $n{=}2$ from $\infty $Bench-Sum.}}{8}{table.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
